    backlog:hasRemedy "Planned into a third iteration, Iter_3, ending at the class of 9 October, proposed from the weekly schedule; the score rationale says the components are proposed for the owner's confirmation, per L-116. Started items carry the earliest time they could have begun, named as a bound." .

ex:Finding_BookPrintedResultMismatch a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "A result the book prints for chapter 3 does not belong to the script above it"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:relatesToWorkItem ex:ST_Research_Ch03, ex:ST_Deck_Ch03, ex:ST_Page_Ch03 ; backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_Methodology ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "Running the chapter's examples on Bitcoin Core 31.1 and its data reproduced everything except one printed result: the text under rpc_block.py reports a block total of 10,322.07722534 BTC including a 25 BTC reward, while the script reads block 775072, whose subsidy under Bitcoin Core's own schedule is 6.25 BTC; the block's outputs sum to 5,863.00566521 BTC in a block explorer's data, and its coinbase is the 6.25 subsidy plus the fees. The printed figure belongs to another block. Found by executing, not by reading." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Chapter 3's deck, page and research record state the discrepancy and show the computation; the book's text is not altered. Reporting it to the book's authors, whose repository is open to issues, is left to the owner." .

ex:Finding_RealSoftwareRunAndVerified a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "The chapter about running Bitcoin Core was checked by running Bitcoin Core"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:relatesToWorkItem ex:ST_Research_Ch03 ; backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_Methodology ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The book's build steps, defaults and printed outputs are for Bitcoin Core 24.0.1; the current release is 31.1, which moved the build to CMake, removed BerkeleyDB wallets, raised the database-cache default and changed fields of the status answers. Reading release notes alone would have left those as claims." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "The 31.1 Linux release was downloaded, its SHA-256 compared with SHA256SUMS and its 11 good signatures counted with builder keys from the guix.sigs repository (the keys' own trust is not established, and the record says so), and run as an offline node in a throw-away home directory; 08-tooling/ch03-evidence holds the script, the outputs and the block data, and the research checks execute against them. The source build itself was not run: the CMake steps rest on the release notes and doc/build-unix.md." .

ex:Finding_PageAndCheckToolingForkedAgain a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "SEN0401's page, gate and check tooling had drifted from SEN0414's and was forked again"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:relatesToWorkItem ex:ST_Research_Ch03, ex:ST_Page_Ch03 ; backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_Methodology ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "For chapter 3 SEN0401 needed the RDODI gate runner, the execution checks and the Word-file writer that only SEN0414 had, and its page test could not run behind a proxy (it replaced the whole environment, dropping HTTPS_PROXY) and its template lacked icons for chapter 3's agents, which the page test refuses. The two courses' pipelines had already diverged: SEN0401's test is ahead of SEN0414's on some checks and behind on others." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Forked again, named as forks: sen0401_rdodi_build_v1_1_0.py (chapter 2 rebuilds byte-identical), sen0401_rdodi_gates_v1_0_0.py, sen0401_rdodi_checks_v1_0_0.py, sen0401_rdodi_docx_v1_0_0.py, page test 9.4.3 (proxy kept) and template 9.4.3 (icons added; earlier entries keep their order). Consolidating the two courses' tooling into one is CME's work and is named here, not done." .

ex:Finding_Stage4ProposedGatesOnChapter3 a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "Stage 4's proposed coverage and substance gates fail on chapter 3's page, as on every published page"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:relatesToWorkItem ex:ST_Page_Ch03 ; backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_Methodology ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "Run over chapter 3's page ABox, RDODI's pipeline validator passes Stage 4's parse, shapes (0 violations, 3 advisory warnings) and source-validity gates and fails two it labels PROPOSED - coverage (10 typed individuals lack a label and content) and substance (108 individuals not substantive); the pedagogy stage passes all its automated gates and refuses only for the owner's pending attestation." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Not remedied and not claimed as passed: the record says which gates pass and which fail. Changing what every page declares is a change to shared tooling and a ruling for the owner." .

ex:Finding_WebReaderRefusals a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "The web reader refused two pages that the shell could read"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:relatesToWorkItem ex:ST_Research_Ch03 ; backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_Methodology ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "For the JSON-LD specification and Bitcoin Core's BIP list the web reader answered that permission had not been given in time." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "The BIP list was read from the Bitcoin Core repository checkout at the pinned commit, and the JSON-LD specification through the environment's proxy from the shell, its title, publication date and abstract read from the page. Both are named as read that way in the research record." .

ex:Finding_BookChapter4Statements a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "Two statements in chapter 4 do not match their primary source or their own rule"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:relatesToWorkItem ex:ST_Research_Ch04, ex:ST_Deck_Ch04, ex:ST_Page_Ch04 ; backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_Methodology ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The book says the secp256k1 curve was established by NIST; SEC 2 from Certicom Research defines it, and that document's Table 2 marks it with a dash in the NIST column (nonconformant with NIST's list) where secp256r1 is recommended. The vanity-address table gives 23 quintillion for eleven characters where 58 to the eleventh is 25 quintillion, and its search times, which follow half the frequency over 100,000 keys a second up to seven characters, are about a third shorter than that rule gives from eight characters on. Everything else of the chapter's worked example reproduced. Found by executing and by reading the standard, not by reading the book alone." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "The deck, page and research record state both, with the computation and the source; the book's text is not altered. Reporting them to the book's authors is left to the owner." .

ex:Finding_ToolkitCheckedAgainstThree a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "The chapter's arithmetic was written down and checked against three independent references"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:relatesToWorkItem ex:ST_Research_Ch04 ; backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_Methodology ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The chapter is arithmetic and encodings; a reader's trust in a recomputation depends on what it was compared with." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "A plain-Python toolkit for secp256k1, HASH160, base58check and bech32/bech32m (08-tooling/ch04-evidence) was compared with Bitcoin Core 31.1 (addresses from public keys and from WIF keys through descriptors, validation of every printed address, error positions), with the book's own reference library, and with all of BIP350's test vectors; exhaustive and random error tests run once and their results saved. The toolkit says it is for reading and not for real funds. RIPEMD-160 comes from the interpreter's OpenSSL, which not every Python build provides." .

ex:Finding_PageTestConceptTapAndIcons a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "Chapter 4's page needed two more shared-tooling changes: a visible click target and four agent icons"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:relatesToWorkItem ex:ST_Page_Ch04 ; backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_Methodology ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The page test's concept-tap step clicked the first term in a subject's text, which for chapter 4 sits in a card that is hidden while one concept is shown, and waited for it until the test timed out; and the template's agent icons had none for randomness, the curve, practice and identifiers, which the page test refuses as a robot is not a role." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Page test 9.4.4 clicks a term the reader can see, and template 9.4.4 adds the four icons after 9.4.3's, keeping the earlier entries in order; the page then passes all 50 checks. Both are forks of shared tooling, to be consolidated by CME." .

