ex:Gap_OutScope_Ch05_14 a backlog:PartialScopeDeclaration ;
    rdfs:label "Out-scoping of the work of this lineage that is not finished"@en ;
    backlog:declaresGapFor ex:Lineage ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:outScopes ex:EP_Deck, ex:EP_Page, ex:EP_Research, ex:Init_Slides, ex:ST_Deck_Ch05, ex:ST_Deck_Ch06, ex:ST_Deck_Ch07, ex:ST_Deck_Ch08, ex:ST_Deck_Ch09, ex:ST_Deck_Ch10, ex:ST_Deck_Ch11, ex:ST_Deck_Ch12, ex:ST_Deck_Ch13, ex:ST_Deck_Ch14, ex:ST_Page_Ch05, ex:ST_Page_Ch06, ex:ST_Page_Ch07, ex:ST_Page_Ch08, ex:ST_Page_Ch09, ex:ST_Page_Ch10, ex:ST_Page_Ch11, ex:ST_Page_Ch12, ex:ST_Page_Ch13, ex:ST_Page_Ch14, ex:ST_Research_Ch05, ex:ST_Research_Ch06, ex:ST_Research_Ch07, ex:ST_Research_Ch08, ex:ST_Research_Ch09, ex:ST_Research_Ch10, ex:ST_Research_Ch11, ex:ST_Research_Ch12, ex:ST_Research_Ch13, ex:ST_Research_Ch14 ;
    backlog:describesUncoveredScope "The deck, research and page stories of chapters 5 to 14 (30 stories) are not Done in this register. Chapters 5, 6 and 7 exist in the course repository but were built outside this register: their stories read Proposed, were never planned, started or recorded here, and recording them Done inside this lineage would be backfilling closed work that was never planned (G23, G105). Chapters 8 to 14 (21 stories) are not built at all. The three epics and the initiative that group the stories are open while any of those stories is open. All of them leave this lineage unchanged and unfinished, so that this lineage closes with no unfinished work inside it; the successor lineage under the same mission takes them in: chapters 5 to 7 by admission with their real finish dates from git and evidence run again, chapters 8 to 14 by admission and ordinary planning. The route is the owner's rule of 2026-10-12 (framework ruling G105: closing unfinished work is not allowed; out-scope it first, close the finished lineage, a successor takes it in), applied to SEN0401 on the instruction given to the course session on 2026-10-14; the owner confirms it by accepting this record." .

ex:Lineage2 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Second lineage run for the SEN0401 decks: the work finished before it was planned, and the chapters still to build"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:lineageOrdinal 2 ; backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Backlogged ;
    backlog:adoptsObligationSet backlog:OS_SDLC_v2 ; backlog:adoptionRecordedAtOpen true .

ex:Succession_Ch05_14 a backlog:LineageSuccession ;
    rdfs:label "Succession that takes in the out-scoped work of chapters 5 to 14"@en ;
    backlog:succeedsLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:successorLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:resolvesGap ex:Gap_OutScope_Ch05_14 ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:successionRationale "The first lineage planned and finished chapters 1 to 4 and the supplementary Numbers page, each with a planning event before its work and evidence after it. Chapters 5 to 7 were built, committed and pushed before they were planned, so the first lineage can neither record them Done (that would add planning events after the work and move finished-late items) nor close with them still Proposed (closing unfinished work is not allowed); chapters 8 to 14 are not built. Restarting it would retract five correct stage outputs and answer a bypass that the order check does not find. The unfinished and unrecorded work was therefore out-scoped in the previous event, this lineage closes complete on what it finished, and a successor under the same mission opens with the Scope of admitting the finished chapters 5 to 7, recorded now with their real finish dates from git, and of building chapters 8 to 14 in the ordinary way. Cost of waiting: the register keeps stating Proposed for finished work and cannot plan chapter 8 honestly; cost of acting: one succession, five stage commits, and evidence run again for nine items; enforcement value forgone: none, the chain of the first lineage stays untouched." .

