ex:ST_Page_Ch08 backlog:hasAuditNote "Agent-reported disclosures for the chapter 8 page (from the course coordinator's relay of the builder's report, not re-verified here), and a change in what passing means: this page passes the page test 9.35.0 (a NEW version; 9.34.0 is untouched, and the chapter check now runs the newest test). Under 9.35.0 four checks no longer fail: the fill-the-blank and write-the-code questions are SKIPPED (the examples hold no number and no Python keyword); the ontology-graph requirement of behaviour kinds is lowered from two kinds to one when the code does not differ; and the ERD label-ratio rule is relaxed from 95 percent to '95 percent or all but one' (this chapter's ERD has 4 labels). Pages 5 to 7 were recorded earlier under 9.34.0 and 9.34.0's rules, so a pass of this page is not the same bar as theirs. Also reported: 45 of 79 examples run in the browser and 34 are Recorded; the question bank was generated with 109 Remember-level items and no Apply items; the test key was used, which proves page logic only; a licence question is open for the CC BY-SA Schnorr portrait on the page." .
ex:Harness2_Page_Ch08 a backlog:TestHarness ; rdfs:label "Chapter check for Page Ch08"@en ; backlog:harnessFor ex:ST_Page_Ch08 ; backlog:hasHarnessEvidence ex:Ev2_Page_Ch08 .
ex:Ev2_Page_Ch08 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Chapter check for Page Ch08"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC_Chapter, ex:AC2_Admission ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "Page/Ch08" ; backlog:hasTestSpec "08-tooling/sen0401_lineage_chapter_check_v1_1_0.py" ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "python3 -B 08-tooling/sen0401_lineage_chapter_check_v1_1_0.py Page/Ch08 > /tmp/claude-0/s/bl_p8/$(echo Page/Ch08 | tr / _).log 2>&1 exited 0 Disclosed by the research run, kept with this evidence: Agent-reported disclosures for the chapter 8 page (from the course coordinator's relay of the builder's report, not re-verified here), and a change in what passing means: this page passes the page test 9.35.0 (a NEW version; 9.34.0 is untouched, and the chapter check now runs the newest test). Under 9.35.0 four checks no longer fail: the fill-the-blank and write-the-code questions are SKIPPED (the examples hold no number and no Python keyword); the ontology-graph requirement of behaviour kinds is lowered from two kinds to one when the code does not differ; and the ERD label-ratio rule is relaxed from 95 percent to '95 percent or all but one' (this chapter's ERD has 4 labels). Pages 5 to 7 were recorded earlier under 9.34.0 and 9.34.0's rules, so a pass of this page is not the same bar as theirs. Also reported: 45 of 79 examples run in the browser and 34 are Recorded; the question bank was generated with 109 Remember-level items and no Apply items; the test key was used, which proves page logic only; a licence question is open for the CC BY-SA Schnorr portrait on the page. (the page test ran against a copy of the page carrying a TEST release key: it proves the page logic, not the instructor's real key)" ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "backlog_evidence_bridge_v1_1_0 with the course repository as workspace" ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-10-15T09:32:46"^^xsd:dateTime .
