ex:ST_Page_Ch10 backlog:hasAuditNote "Agent-reported disclosures for the chapter 10 page (from the course coordinator's relay of the builder's report, not re-verified here). The chapter check ran the newest page test, 9.35.0, and passed. The builder reports that 9.34.0 gives 368 passed, 0 failed and 2 skips that are inside 9.34.0 itself (the ERD label overlap check and the labels-on-choice mode are skipped because the research states no relation between two sections). 49 of 62 examples run in the browser and 13 are Recorded. Third-party texts are left out of the wheel and their examples Recorded: the Bitnodes census snapshot, Blockchain.com and mempool.space data, Heilman 2015, Apostolaki 2017, a 2016 bloom-filter list post, and the bitcoinfibre.org page. Embedded, clear: Bitcoin Core (MIT), the book (CC BY-SA 4.0), the BIPs, Optech (CC BY 4.0), the Bitcoin paper (MIT), the course run record. Known research defect: the stored output of OrphanageLimits was mangled by the builder's quote rule while the page shows the real one; a research fix (1_0_1) is queued. The test key was used, which proves page logic only. The page is 3.26 MB and its longest task is 152 ms." .
ex:Harness2_Page_Ch10 a backlog:TestHarness ; rdfs:label "Chapter check for Page Ch10"@en ; backlog:harnessFor ex:ST_Page_Ch10 ; backlog:hasHarnessEvidence ex:Ev2_Page_Ch10 .
ex:Ev2_Page_Ch10 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Chapter check for Page Ch10"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC_Chapter, ex:AC2_Admission ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "Page/Ch10" ; backlog:hasTestSpec "08-tooling/sen0401_lineage_chapter_check_v1_1_0.py" ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "python3 -B 08-tooling/sen0401_lineage_chapter_check_v1_1_0.py Page/Ch10 > /tmp/claude-0/s/bl_p10/$(echo Page/Ch10 | tr / _).log 2>&1 exited 0 Disclosed by the research run, kept with this evidence: Agent-reported disclosures for the chapter 10 page (from the course coordinator's relay of the builder's report, not re-verified here). The chapter check ran the newest page test, 9.35.0, and passed. The builder reports that 9.34.0 gives 368 passed, 0 failed and 2 skips that are inside 9.34.0 itself (the ERD label overlap check and the labels-on-choice mode are skipped because the research states no relation between two sections). 49 of 62 examples run in the browser and 13 are Recorded. Third-party texts are left out of the wheel and their examples Recorded: the Bitnodes census snapshot, Blockchain.com and mempool.space data, Heilman 2015, Apostolaki 2017, a 2016 bloom-filter list post, and the bitcoinfibre.org page. Embedded, clear: Bitcoin Core (MIT), the book (CC BY-SA 4.0), the BIPs, Optech (CC BY 4.0), the Bitcoin paper (MIT), the course run record. Known research defect: the stored output of OrphanageLimits was mangled by the builder's quote rule while the page shows the real one; a research fix (1_0_1) is queued. The test key was used, which proves page logic only. The page is 3.26 MB and its longest task is 152 ms. (the page test ran against a copy of the page carrying a TEST release key: it proves the page logic, not the instructor's real key)" ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "backlog_evidence_bridge_v1_1_0 with the course repository as workspace" ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-10-15T14:11:54"^^xsd:dateTime .
